  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://w3id.org/ad4gd/ev/ebv/ES_edis_MA_ecosystemProductivity_RESP">
    <skos:definition>Productivity in an ecosystem refers to the percentage of energy that enters the ecosystem in the form of biomass at a particular trophic level. It is the rate at which biomass is formed in the ecosystem. Respiration.</skos:definition>
